speechtext:
Mr. Speaker, there have been discussions between House Leaders and I believe that if you were to present the following motion, you would find it would pass by unanimous consent without debate. The motions is as follows:
That, notwithstanding any Standing or Special Order of this House, the Order of Reference to a legislative committee of Bill C-71, An Act to amend the Customs Tariff, shall be discharged and the said Bill shall stand referred to a Committee of the Whole for consideration as the first item of business under Government Orders later this day;
Provided that not later than 15 minutes before the end of the time provided for the consideration of Government Business this day, the Speaker shall interrupt, if necessary, any proceedings then before the House and shall put forthwith all questions necessary to dispose of the then remaining stages of the said Bill without further debate or amendment;
That when the motion for the third reading and passage of Bill C-71, An Act to amend the Customs Tariff, has been disposed of, the House shall proceed to consideration of the motion for the second reading and reference to a legislative committee of Bill C-72, An Act to amend the statute law relating to income tax and to make a related amendment to the Tax Court of Canada Act, and when disposed of at the second reading stage the same shall stand referred to a Committee of the Whole;
Provided, that not later than the end of time provided for the consideration of Government Business this day, the Speaker shall interrupt, if necessary, any proceedings then before the House and shall put forthwith, all questions necessary to dispose of the remaining stages of the said Bill without further debate or amendment.
